{"name":"Sign of the Crown","hex":"#fce299","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sign","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A visible fact that shows that something exists or may happen.","An omen."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a mark\n To seal (a document etc.) with an identifying seal or symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To seal (a document etc.) with an identifying seal or symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sign"},{"term":"crown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal, imperial or princely headdress; a diadem.","A wreath or band for the head, especially one given as reward of victory or a mark of honor."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, related to, or pertaining to a crown.","Of, related to, pertaining to the top of a tree or trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sign","blocks":[{"text":"A sign is an object, quality, event, or entity whose presence or occurrence indicates the probable presence or occurrence of something else. A natural sign bears a causal relation to its object—for instance, thunder is a sign of storm, or medical symptoms a sign of disease. A conventional sign signifies by agreement, as a full stop signifies the end of a sentence; similarly the words and expressions of a language, which can be interpreted as bodily gestures, can be regarded as signs, expressing particular meanings. The physical objects most commonly referred to as signs generally inform or instruct using written text, symbols, pictures or a combination of these."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Biohazard.svg/330px-Biohazard.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sign"},{"title":"Crown","blocks":[{"text":"A crown is a traditional form of head adornment, or hat, worn by monarchs as a symbol of their power and dignity. A crown is often, by extension, a symbol of the monarch's government or items endorsed by it. The word itself is used, particularly in Commonwealth countries, as an abstract name for the monarchy itself as distinct from the individual who inhabits it. A specific type of crown is employed in heraldry under strict rules. Indeed, some monarchies never had a physical crown, just a heraldic representation, to wit the constitutional kingdom of Belgium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Saint_Edward%27s_Crown.jpg/330px-Saint_Edward%27s_Crown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/LGA_recheck_compass_jeh.jpg/500px-LGA_recheck_compass_jeh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/LGA_recheck_compass_jeh.jpg/1280px-LGA_recheck_compass_jeh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/LGA_recheck_compass_jeh.jpg/500px-LGA_recheck_compass_jeh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" An airport sign at La Guardia Airport","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALGA_recheck_compass_jeh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Big_Foot_%286225546731%29.jpg/500px-Big_Foot_%286225546731%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Big_Foot_%286225546731%29.jpg/500px-Big_Foot_%286225546731%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A natural sign in the environment indicating recent human activity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3